{"cuisine/colombian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/colombian-cuisine","n":"Colombian cuisine","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Colombia","intro":[["Colombian cuisine is a culinary tradition of six main regions within Colombia: Insular, Caribbean, Pacific, Andean, Orinoco, and Amazonian. Colombian cuisine varies regionally and is influenced by Indigenous Colombian, Spanish, and African cuisines, with a slight Arab influence in some regions."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"colombian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colombian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"My Colombian Recipes","ref":"site/mycolombianrecipes-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"mycolombianrecipes.com","note":"Medellín-born Erica Dinho's blog of traditional Colombian recipes.","url":"https://www.mycolombianrecipes.com/about/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Colombiana: A Rediscovery of Recipes and Rituals from the Soul of Colombia","ref":"cookbook/colombiana-a-rediscovery-of-recipes-and-rituals-from-the-soul-of-colombia","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Mariana Velásquez, 2021","note":"Bogotá-born food stylist's tour of Colombian regional cooking.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9780063019430","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":6,"links":[["Arepa","dish/arepa"],["Calentao","dish/calentao"],["Cholado","dish/cholado"],["Pandebono","dish/pandebono"],["Puchero","dish/puchero"],["Pueblito Viejo","dish/pueblito-viejo"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Cornmeal","ingredient/cornmeal"],["Maize flour","ingredient/maize-flour"],["Maize meal","ingredient/maize-meal"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Cassava","ingredient/cassava"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Corn starch","ingredient/corn-starch"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Starch","ingredient/starch"],["Bacon","ingredient/bacon"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Pasta","ingredient/pasta"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Turnip","ingredient/turnip"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Within Colombian cooking","count":1,"links":[["Muisca cuisine","cuisine/muisca-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from Colombia","count":1,"links":[["Wayuu foodways","cuisine/wayuu-foodways"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas"},"cuisine/ou-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/ou-cuisine","n":"Ou cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in China","intro":[["Ou cuisine, alternatively known as Wenzhou cuisine, is one of the four schools of Zhejiang cuisine, whereas Zhejiang cuisine is one of the eight major cuisines in China. The ancient name of Wenzhou is Dong'ou. After the founding of the People’s Republic of China, in order to improve the popularity of Wenzhou cuisine, catering experts has renamed the cuisine with its ancient name, \"Ou cai\". The major elements in Ou cuisine are seafood, which tastes fresh, light, and not bland. During the cooking process, it emphasizes \"two light and a heavy,\" that is, light oil, light thickening, and heavy knife action, and it has a noticeable distinctive style."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ou-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ou_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine"},"dish/63-clinton":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/63-clinton","n":"63 Clinton","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from New American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["63 Clinton (sometimes Sixty Three Clinton) is a restaurant in New York City on the Lower East Side. The two chefs behind the restaurant, Sam Clonts and Raymond Trinh used to work at Bar Uchū. The seasonal American cuisine menu with global influences solely consists of a 7-course seasonal tasting menu with an optional extra caviar hand roll with the one dish common amongst all seasons being the breakfast taco with an ajitama egg, salsa verde, and trout roe. The restaurant has received a Michelin star."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-63-clinton"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/63_Clinton"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["New American cuisine","cuisine/new-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from New American cuisine","links":[["Benu (restaurant)","dish/benu-restaurant"],["Boka (restaurant)","dish/boka-restaurant"],["Boulevard (restaurant)","dish/boulevard-restaurant"],["Cafe La Haye","dish/cafe-la-haye"],["Canlis","dish/canlis"],["Clinton Street Baking Company & Restaurant","dish/clinton-street-baking-company-restaurant"],["Elements (restaurant)","dish/elements-restaurant"],["Four Seasons Restaurant","dish/four-seasons-restaurant"],["Gotham Bar and Grill","dish/gotham-bar-and-grill"],["Gramercy Tavern","dish/gramercy-tavern"],["Harvest Moon Cafe","dish/harvest-moon-cafe"],["King's Carriage House","dish/king-s-carriage-house"],["Laurelhurst Market","dish/laurelhurst-market"],["Montrio Bistro","dish/montrio-bistro"],["Moody Tongue","dish/moody-tongue"],["Peacock Inn (Princeton, New Jersey)","dish/peacock-inn-princeton-new-jersey"],["Rich Table","dish/rich-table"],["Saison (restaurant)","dish/saison-restaurant"],["Somni","dish/somni"],["Sons & Daughters (restaurant)","dish/sons-daughters-restaurant"],["State Bird Provisions","dish/state-bird-provisions"],["The Musket Room","dish/the-musket-room"],["Union Square Cafe","dish/union-square-cafe"],["Woodberry Kitchen","dish/woodberry-kitchen"]]}]},"dish/barbetta":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/barbetta","n":"Barbetta","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Barbetta was an Italian restaurant that focused on Piedmontese cuisine located at 321 West 46th Street (between 8th Avenue and 9th Avenue) on the Theater District's Restaurant Row in New York City. Founded in 1906, Barbetta was one of the city's oldest family-owned Italian restaurants was and the oldest restaurant in the Theater District. It held many other firsts from its food innovations."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-barbetta"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbetta"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","ref":"site/pastagrannies-substack-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","ref":"site/recipesfromitaly-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and course.","url":"https://recipesfromitaly.com","suggested":true},{"name":"Manu's Menu","ref":"site/manusmenu-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"manusmenu.com","note":"Italian-born home cook Manuela sharing classic family and regional Italian dishes.","url":"https://www.manusmenu.com/about/about-this-site","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Italian cuisine","links":[["8½ Otto e Mezzo Bombana","dish/8-otto-e-mezzo-bombana"],["A16 (restaurant)","dish/a16-restaurant"],["Acquacotta","dish/acquacotta"],["Agliata","dish/agliata"],["Agnolotti","dish/agnolotti"],["Alfredo alla Scrofa","dish/alfredo-alla-scrofa"],["Alioto's","dish/alioto-s"],["Amalfi's Italian Restaurant","dish/amalfi-s-italian-restaurant"],["Amato's","dish/amato-s"],["Angelo's Civita Farnese","dish/angelo-s-civita-farnese"],["Antica Pizzeria Port'Alba"